<%# == Suite growth over time
        The Overview above answers "+47 since the last run" — one subtraction across two rows. This
        answers what the suite has done over the last thirty runs, which `test_runs` has been able
        to say since Phase 2 and nothing has ever asked.

        Built on the BRANCH history (`Repository#suite_size_trajectory`), never on the "Recent runs"
        panel below, which is one interleaved history across every branch and disclaims being a
        series in those exact words. A line drawn through that panel's rows would connect a trunk
        run to a feature branch's and call the gap growth.

        Outside the `manage_keys` gate for the same reason the Overview and Recent runs are: read-
        only suite telemetry, nothing credential, nothing actionable.

        Not rendered at all when CI has never reported. The Overview's "No CI run has reported yet"
        is the page's one never-ingested empty state, and a second dashed box saying a quieter
        version of it would read as a different, milder fact. %>
<% if @latest_test_run.present? %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Suite growth", id: "suite-trajectory") do %>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <% if @suite_trajectory.branch.blank? %>
            <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                  title: "No branch to plot a history on",
                  description: "The latest run named no branch, so SpecGuard cannot place it in one. " \
                               "Runs that name no branch are not pooled together — they may come from " \
                               "anywhere, and a line drawn through them would be a history of nothing " \
                               "in particular."
                ) %>
          <% elsif @suite_trajectory.plottable? %>
            <% trajectory_points = @suite_trajectory.plotted.map do |run|
                 UI::SparklineComponent::Point.new(
                   label: run.commit_sha.first(7),
                   value: run.total_specs_count.to_i,
                   detail: "#{time_ago_in_words(run.created_at)} ago"
                 )
               end %>
            <%= render UI::SparklineComponent.new(
                  id: "suite-trajectory-chart",
                  points: trajectory_points,
                  label: "Tests in suite on #{@suite_trajectory.branch}",
                  coverage: @suite_trajectory.coverage,
                  summary: "The suite measured between #{number_with_delimiter(@suite_trajectory.minimum)} " \
                           "and #{number_with_delimiter(@suite_trajectory.maximum)} tests across " \
                           "#{@suite_trajectory.plotted.size} runs on #{@suite_trajectory.branch}, " \
                           "the oldest #{time_ago_in_words(@suite_trajectory.first_run.created_at)} ago " \
                           "and the newest #{time_ago_in_words(@suite_trajectory.last_run.created_at)} ago. " \
                           "The vertical axis spans that range and does not start at zero, so the " \
                           "slope is the size of the change and not its share of the suite.",
                  columns: ["Run", "Tests in suite", "Ingested"],
                  formatter: trajectory_size_formatter,
                  point_formatter: trajectory_size_point_formatter
                ) %>
            <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "suite-trajectory-basis") do %>
              Drawn through <%= @suite_trajectory.plotted.size %>
              of the last <%= @suite_trajectory.considered_count %>
              <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.considered_count) %>
              on <%= @suite_trajectory.branch %><%= ", #{@suite_trajectory.cohort_description}" if @suite_trajectory.cohort_description %>,
              covering <%= distance_of_time_in_words(@suite_trajectory.first_run.created_at,
                                                     @suite_trajectory.last_run.created_at) %>.
              Only runs on the same branch are plotted — a suite size from somewhere else is not a
              change this branch made.
              <% if @suite_trajectory.flat? %>
                Every one of them measured
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@suite_trajectory.minimum) %> tests: this suite has not
                moved over that window, which is a measurement and not an absence of one.
              <% end %>
              <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_unmeasured.any? %>
                <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_unmeasured.size %>
                <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.withheld_unmeasured.size) %>
                <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_unmeasured.size == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> withheld for
                having reported no tests at all — a zero there describes the report, not the suite.
              <% end %>
              <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_part_way.any? %>
                <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_part_way.size %>
                <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.withheld_part_way.size) %>
                <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_part_way.size == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> withheld for
                having reported only some of the parts the plotted runs reported: a run's test
                count is the sum of the shards it has reported so far, so a build still arriving —
                or one cancelled part-way — sits at a fraction of its own suite, and plotting it
                beside a complete run would draw a drop no commit made.
              <% end %>
              <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_other_composition.any? %>
                <% others = @suite_trajectory.withheld_other_composition %>
                <% others_delivery = @suite_trajectory.shared_delivery_description(others) %>
                <%= others.size %>
                <%= "run".pluralize(others.size) %>
                <%= others.size == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> withheld for having arrived differently from
                the runs the line is drawn through<%= " — #{others_delivery}, where the line is drawn through runs #{@suite_trajectory.cohort_delivery}" if others_delivery %>.
                A total counts the work that was delivered, so two runs assembled from different
                numbers of parts cannot be differenced in either direction. That is not a claim
                that these ones measured less than they should have.
              <% end %>
              <% unless @suite_trajectory.plots_newest? %>
                The most recent run on <%= @suite_trajectory.branch %> is not on this line:
                <span class="font-mono"><%= @suite_trajectory.newest_run.commit_sha.first(7) %></span>
                is one of the withheld runs, so the line ends at
                <span class="font-mono"><%= @suite_trajectory.last_run.commit_sha.first(7) %></span>,
                <%= time_ago_in_words(@suite_trajectory.last_run.created_at) %> ago.
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
            <% if @suite_trajectory.runtime_plottable? %>
              <% runtime_formatter = trajectory_runtime_formatter %>
              <% runtime_points = @suite_trajectory.timed.map do |run|
                   UI::SparklineComponent::Point.new(
                     label: run.commit_sha.first(7),
                     value: run.duration_seconds.to_f,
                     detail: "#{time_ago_in_words(run.created_at)} ago"
                   )
                 end %>
              <%= render UI::SparklineComponent.new(
                    id: "suite-trajectory-runtime-chart",
                    points: runtime_points,
                    label: "Wall clock on #{@suite_trajectory.branch}",
                    coverage: @suite_trajectory.runtime_coverage,
                    summary: "These runs waited between #{runtime_formatter.call(@suite_trajectory.runtime_minimum)} " \
                             "and #{runtime_formatter.call(@suite_trajectory.runtime_maximum)} across " \
                             "#{@suite_trajectory.timed.size} runs on #{@suite_trajectory.branch}, " \
                             "the oldest #{time_ago_in_words(@suite_trajectory.first_timed_run.created_at)} ago " \
                             "and the newest #{time_ago_in_words(@suite_trajectory.last_timed_run.created_at)} ago. " \
                             "Each point is the run's wall clock — the slowest single shard, not the " \
                             "machine time the suite cost. The vertical axis spans that range and does " \
                             "not start at zero, so the slope is the size of the change and not its " \
                             "share of the wait.",
                    columns: ["Run", "Wall clock", "Ingested"],
                    formatter: runtime_formatter
                  ) %>
              <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "suite-trajectory-runtime-basis") do %>
                Drawn through <%= @suite_trajectory.timed.size %>
                of the <%= @suite_trajectory.plotted.size %>
                <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.plotted.size) %>
                the suite-size line is drawn through, on <%= @suite_trajectory.branch %><%= ", #{@suite_trajectory.cohort_description}" if @suite_trajectory.cohort_description %>.
                Each point is that run's wall clock — how long the build waited, which on a sharded
                run is its slowest single shard and not the machine time every shard spent. Only
                runs assembled the same way and timed over the same number of shards are plotted:
                a config that splits four shards into eight halves the wall clock without anything
                having got faster, and so does a run whose two slowest shards were cancelled before
                they reported.
                <% if @suite_trajectory.runtime_flat? %>
                  Every one of them waited
                  <%= runtime_formatter.call(@suite_trajectory.runtime_minimum) %>: this suite's
                  wall clock has not moved over that window, which is a measurement and not an
                  absence of one.
                <% end %>
                <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_untimed.any? %>
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_untimed.size %>
                  <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.withheld_untimed.size) %>
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_untimed.size == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> withheld from
                  this line for having reported no timing at all, and
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_untimed.size == 1 ? "remains" : "remain" %>
                  on the suite-size line above: a missing wall clock is something the client did not
                  send, not a build that took no time.
                <% end %>
                <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.any? %>
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.size %>
                  <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.size) %>
                  reported a wall clock over a different number of shards than the runs on this
                  line, so
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.size == 1 ? "it is" : "they are" %>
                  withheld from it and
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.size == 1 ? "remains" : "remain" %>
                  on the suite-size line above: a wall clock is the slowest shard that reported, so
                  two runs whose shards reported in different numbers cannot be differenced without
                  reading telemetry loss as a change in speed.
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            <% else %>
              <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "suite-trajectory-runtime-basis") do %>
                No wall-clock line yet on <%= @suite_trajectory.branch %>:
                <% if @suite_trajectory.timed.empty? %>
                  none of the <%= @suite_trajectory.plotted.size %> plotted
                  <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.plotted.size) %> reported one.
                <% else %>
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.timed.size %> of the
                  <%= @suite_trajectory.plotted.size %> plotted
                  <%= "run".pluralize(@suite_trajectory.plotted.size) %>
                  <% if @suite_trajectory.withheld_timing_mismatch.any? %>
                    timed the same number of shards — a wall clock is the slowest shard that
                    reported, so runs whose shards reported in different numbers are not one line —
                    and a trajectory needs
                  <% else %>
                    reported one, and a trajectory needs
                  <% end %>
                  <%= SuiteTrajectory::MINIMUM_POINTS %>.
                <% end %>
                A single wall clock drawn as a line is a flat one, which says this suite takes as
                long as it always did — a claim one measurement cannot support.
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          <% else %>
            <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                  title: "Not enough comparable runs yet",
                  description: trajectory_thin_description(@suite_trajectory)
                ) %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
